1 SUBMIT

   Enters one or more command procedures in a batch queue as a job.  The
   job runs, as a detached process logged in to your account (or the one
   /USER names), when its time comes and the queue has room.  SUBMIT
   says what it did, and defines the local symbol $ENTRY as the job's
   entry number.

   Format

     SUBMIT file-spec[,...]

2 Parameter

 file-spec[,...]

   The command procedures the job runs, in order; the default type is
   .COM, and a wildcard enters every file it finds.  Files separated by
   commas or plus signs are all one job's.  The job holds each file by
   its file ID, so a later version doesn't take its place.

2 Description

   The queue must exist and you need submit access to it (S, by its
   protection or ACL; %SUBMIT-F-CREJOB with -JBC-E-NOPRIV).  A missing
   file is %SUBMIT-F-OPENIN, a missing queue -JBC-E-NOSUCHQUE.

   SUBMIT's report is one of

     Job name (queue q, entry n) pending
          pending status caused by queue stopped state
     Job name (queue q, entry n) holding
     Job name (queue q, entry n) holding until dd-mmm-yyyy hh:mm

   SHOW ENTRY and SHOW QUEUE show the job; SET ENTRY changes it, and
   DELETE/ENTRY deletes it.  govax has no print queues, so a job's log
   file is kept on disk.

2 Qualifiers
/AFTER

      /AFTER=time

   Holds the job until the time: an absolute time, TODAY, TOMORROW, a
   delta from now ("+0:30"), or a combination ("TOMORROW+12:00").  A
   time already past makes the job pending at once.

/CPUTIME

      /CPUTIME=limit

   The job's CPU time limit: hh:mm:ss, NONE (the queue's default), or
   INFINITE.  It may not be more than the queue's /CPUMAXIMUM.

/DELETE

   Deletes the files when the job has run them.

/HOLD

   Holds the job until SET ENTRY/RELEASE.  With /AFTER the job is
   holding, and its release makes it pending at once.

/IDENTIFY

      /[NO]IDENTIFY

   Says what SUBMIT did (the default); /NOIDENTIFY says nothing.

/KEEP

      /[NO]KEEP

   Keeps the job's log file after the job (the default, since govax has
   no print queues); /NOKEEP deletes it.

/LOG_FILE

      /[NO]LOG_FILE[=file-spec]

   The job's log file.  The default is SYS$LOGIN:jobname.LOG; a
   directory alone takes the job's name, a name alone goes in
   SYS$LOGIN.  The directory must exist (%SUBMIT-F-INVLOGFIL).
   /NOLOG_FILE keeps no log.

/NAME

      /NAME=job-name

   The job's name; the default is the first file's name.

/NOTE

      /NOTE="text"

   A note SHOW ENTRY/FULL shows with the job.

/NOTIFY

   Tells you at your terminal when the job ends.

/PARAMETERS

      /PARAMETERS=(p1[,...])

   Up to eight values, P1 to P8 in each of the job's files.  An
   unquoted value is uppercased; a quoted one keeps its case.

/PRINTER

      /[NO]PRINTER[=queue]

   VMS prints the log on a print queue.  govax has none: /PRINTER=queue
   is %SUBMIT-F-CREJOB with -JBC-E-NODSTQUE, and /NOPRINTER (or no
   /PRINTER) keeps the log.

/PRIORITY

      /PRIORITY=n

   The job's place in its queue, 0 to 255 (default 100), not its
   process's priority.  Above 100 needs OPER or ALTPRI; without them the
   priority is lowered to 100 with %JBC-I-PRIOSMALL.

/QUEUE

      /QUEUE=queue-name

   The queue; the default is SYS$BATCH.

/RESTART

   Restarts the job, rather than ending it, if govax stops while it
   runs.

/RETAIN

      /[NO]RETAIN[=option]

   Keeps the job in its queue when it ends: ALWAYS (the default
   option), ERROR (if it fails), or UNTIL=time.  /NORETAIN keeps it
   whatever the queue says.

/USER

      /USER=username

   Runs the job as another account.  It needs CMKRNL (-JBC-E-NOCMKRNL)
   and read access to the authorization file; an account that isn't
   there, or a file you can't read, is %SUBMIT-F-INVQUAVAL.

/WSDEFAULT

      /WSDEFAULT=n

   The job's working-set default, in pages: kept and shown.

/WSEXTENT

      /WSEXTENT=n

   The job's working-set extent, in pages: kept and shown.

/WSQUOTA

      /WSQUOTA=n

   The job's working-set quota, in pages: kept and shown.

2 Examples

   1.$ SUBMIT/QUEUE=SYS$BATCH/AFTER=TOMORROW/PARAMETERS=(FULL) NIGHTLY
     Job NIGHTLY (queue SYS$BATCH, entry 21) holding until 17-NOV-2026 00:00

     Enters NIGHTLY.COM to run at midnight, with P1 FULL.

   2.$ SUBMIT/HOLD/NAME=BUILD STEP1,STEP2
     Job BUILD (queue SYS$BATCH, entry 22) holding
     $ SET ENTRY '$ENTRY'/RELEASE

     Enters a job of two files, held, then releases it.
